"ACPErrorSSHNotFoundDetail" -> "Install the OpenSSH client, or give the path of ssh with \"Executable\" in the \"SSHSettings\" setting.",
"ACPErrorSSHNotFoundDetailWindows" -> "Install the OpenSSH Client (type Optional features in the Start menu search, then add OpenSSH Client), or give the path of ssh.exe with \"Executable\" in the \"SSHSettings\" setting.",
"ACPErrorSSHNotFoundPath" -> "`path` was not found or is not executable on this computer.",
"ACPErrorSSHNotFoundPathDetail" -> "Check \"Executable\" in the \"SSHSettings\" setting: it must be the path or the name of the ssh program on this computer (Automatic finds ssh).",
"ACPErrorSSHStartFailed" -> "Couldn't start ssh.",
"ACPErrorSSHHostKeyUnknown" -> "`host` is not a known host yet.",
"ACPErrorSSHHostKeyUnknownDetail" -> "Connect to it once in a terminal with `command`, check that the host key fingerprint is the server's and accept it, then reconnect. Agent chats always check host keys: if your ssh configuration turns host key checking off for this host (StrictHostKeyChecking no, UserKnownHostsFile /dev/null), keep its key in your known_hosts file instead.",
"ACPErrorSSHHostKeyChanged" -> "The host key of `host` has changed.",
"ACPErrorSSHHostKeyChangedDetail" -> "This can mean that someone is intercepting the connection, or that the server was reinstalled. Check the new key with the server's administrator before you change your known_hosts file.",
"ACPErrorSSHAuthFailed" -> "`host` didn't accept your SSH key.",
"ACPErrorSSHAuthFailedDetail" -> "Agent chats sign in without prompts: use a key that is loaded in your SSH agent or has no passphrase, and give its file with \"Arguments\" -> {\"-i\", \"path\"} in the \"SSHSettings\" setting if it is not a default key.",
"ACPErrorSSHKeyPermissionsDetail" -> "ssh ignores the key file because other users can read it. Restrict its permissions to your user account.",
"ACPErrorSSHKeyMissingDetail" -> "ssh couldn't find the key file given with \"-i\".",
"ACPErrorSSHHostNotFound" -> "The host `host` was not found.",
"ACPErrorSSHHostNotFoundDetail" -> "Check \"MachineName\" in the \"SSHSettings\" setting and your network connection.",
"ACPErrorSSHConnectionRefused" -> "`host` refused the connection.",
"ACPErrorSSHConnectionRefusedDetail" -> "Check that its SSH server is running and that the port is right (for another port: \"Arguments\" -> {\"-p\", \"<port>\"}).",
